ion 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A has completed two-third of a job in 8 days, and B completes the rest of the job in 20 days. In how many days can they together complete the job?", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "The radius and height of a cone are 4 cm and 3 cm, respectively. Find the volume of the cone.", "options": [{"text": "12π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "16π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "8π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "48π cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "If Ram gets a discount of 12% on the marked price of a fan, he saves ₹600. How much did Ram pay for the fan?", "options": [{"text": "₹4,400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,300", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,600", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Twin prime numbers are the prime numbers whose difference is always equal to 2. The number of twin primes between 35 and 100 is:", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "types-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "A 300 m long train crosses a platform which is five times of its length, in 7 minutes 40 sec. What is the speed of the train?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Three numbers which are co-prime to each other are such that the product of the first two is 391 and that of the last two is 943. Find the middle number.", "options": [{"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "19", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "factors-divisors", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "What is the average of the following numbers? 4, 3, 7, −3, 0, −5, −7, 5, −6, 0, −4, 6", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "What is the smallest number which, when divided by 15, 17 and 19, leaves remainder 4, 6 and 8, respectively?", "options": [{"text": "4845", "added": false}, {"text": "4548", "added": false}, {"text": "4832", "added": false}, {"text": "4834", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "remainder-based", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Venu invested a certain amount in shares. The shares rose by 25% on the first day, fell by 8% on the second day and fell by 10% the next day. The percentage profit or loss made by Venu is:", "options": [{"text": "4.5%, profit", "added": false}, {"text": "4.5%, loss", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5%, profit", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5%, loss", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}]}